    "encrypted": "false",
    "display_name": "Handle Empty Results",
    "long_instructions": "# Handle Empty Results\r\n\r\n**Goal:** Show a helpful message when your API returns zero results or invalid data.\r\n\r\n1. **Check the Response Data:** After your fetch completes, check if the returned array is empty.\r\n2. **Display an Empty State Message:** Show a friendly message such as \"No results found\" instead of leaving the page blank.\r\n3. **Keep the Layout Stable:** Make sure your app still looks clean and organized when showing the empty message.\r\n4. **Test It:** Modify your endpoint or search input to force zero results and confirm the message appears.\r\n5. **Remove the Message When Data Exists:** If results return again, hide the empty state message.\r\n\r\n",
    "bubble_choice_description": "Display a clear message when no data is returned so users understand what happened instead of seeing a blank screen. ***(supports completing Milestone 3 tasks)***",
